<%
# ============================================================================
# THE LOCKPICK GAUNTLET - SCENARIO FILE
# ============================================================================
# Break Escape - SAFETYNET physical-entry training range
#
# A long sequence of rooms split into two phases:
#
#   PHASE 1 — PICKING: eight pin-tumbler doors of slowly increasing
#   lockpicking difficulty. Mirrors the old locksmith-forge level curve:
#   pin count climbs 3 -> 8, tolerances tighten tutorial -> easy -> medium
#   -> hard. The player carries ONLY a lockpick set, so each door routes
#   straight to the lockpicking mini-game.
#
#   PHASE 2 — KEY SELECTION: three "key rooms". Each room holds THREE keys,
#   only one of which is cut to open that room's forward door. This mirrors
#   the locksmith-forge "key mode" (config.keyMode / startWithKeySelection):
#   once the player is carrying key items, the door opens the key-selection
#   mini-game and they must pick the key whose bitting matches the lock.
#   (Picks are run first, before any key is collected, because carrying keys
#   makes every later door default to key-selection in the engine.)
#
# ROOM LAYOUT (linear vertical climb, north = deeper into the range):
#   Antechamber (lockpick set)
#     -> Gate 1 (pick, 3 pins, tutorial)
#       -> ... -> Gate 7 (pick, 7 pins, hard)
#         -> Key Room A: pick 8-pin door to enter; holds 3 four-cut keys
#           -> Keyed Door 1 (4 pins, KEY SELECTION); holds 3 six-cut keys
#             -> Keyed Door 2 (6 pins, KEY SELECTION); holds 3 eight-cut keys
#               -> Vault (8 pins, KEY SELECTION) -> recover trophy -> SUCCESS
#
# In each key room, the CORRECT key's keyPins exactly match the forward
# door's keyPins (so its cuts align); the two decoys share the same number
# of cuts but a different bitting, so they will not turn the lock.
# ============================================================================
%>
